FONTLOG for the Passerelle Baton font

This file provides detailed information on the Passerelle Baton Font Software.
This information should be distributed along with the Passerelle Baton fonts and any derivative works.

Basic Font Information
Passerelle Baton is a cursive and script font designed for handwriting instruction in primary schools. This derivative version brings specific adjustments to meet the educational needs of primary school teachers.
Passerelle Baton is a modified version of the original Marelle font, initially developed by the French Ministry of National Education.

ChangeLog
20 May 2026 (Delphine Rimbaud-Le Borgne, Laurence Pierson, Khalid Kharbouche) Passerelle Baton v1.100
- Replaced the open "s" from the initial version with the alternative closed "s" from the original character set.
- Changed the uppercase letters size from 2 to 3 interlines.
- Modified strokes for better weight consistency and to facilitate drawing for students, particularly for letters G, K, M, W, and Y.
- Changed font name to respect the Reserved Font Name clause: "Marelle Bâton" becomes "Passerelle Baton".
- Cleaned, updated, and synchronized identification metadata in PostScript (PS Names) and TrueType (TTF Names) tables in FontForge.

